## 8.1 Technology Stack

### Frontend

- React.js.
- Vite.
- JavaScript or TypeScript.
- React Router.
- Tailwind CSS.
- Axios or Fetch API.

### Backend

- Node.js.
- Express.js.
- JavaScript or TypeScript.
- REST API.

### Database

- MongoDB.
- Mongoose.

### AI

- Google Gemini API.
- Server-side AI service.

### Media Storage

- Cloudinary or another configurable media-storage provider.

### Authentication

Authentication is optional for the first MVP.

The MVP may support guest sessions with persistent case IDs.

If authentication is added, use secure authentication practices and associate cases with the authenticated user.

## 8.2 High-Level Architecture

Frontend (React)

↓

Backend API (Express)

↓

Application Services

- Mystery Service
- AI Service
- Evidence Service
- Case Resolution Service

↓

MongoDB

↓

Gemini API / Media Provider

## 8.3 Backend Design Principles

- Keep business logic out of frontend components.
- Keep AI prompts in a dedicated prompt module.
- Keep Gemini integration in a dedicated AI service.
- Keep database operations in model or repository modules.
- Validate all incoming requests.
- Validate all AI-generated output.
- Keep the actual culprit and solution server-side.
- Never trust user-submitted suspect IDs without validating them against the case.
- Keep media provider integration separate from mystery-generation logic.

