# 12. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

The backend must:

- Store API keys in environment variables.
- Validate all request inputs.
- Limit request sizes.
- Apply rate limiting to AI generation.
- Prevent duplicate generation requests.
- Validate MongoDB IDs.
- Prevent unauthorized access to cases.
- Avoid exposing hidden solution fields.
- Handle Gemini errors safely.
- Avoid logging API keys or sensitive data.

The frontend must never contain the Gemini API key.

The application must not execute generated AI content as code.

Generated HTML or scripts must not be inserted into the page using unsafe rendering mechanisms.

---

# 13. ERROR HANDLING

The system must handle:

### AI Generation Failure

Display:

"Unable to generate your mystery right now. Please try again."

### Invalid AI Response

Attempt a limited regeneration or repair.

### Database Failure

Return a generic server error and log the internal details.

### Invalid Case ID

Return a 404 response.

### Invalid Suspect ID

Return a 400 response.

### Already Resolved Case

Prevent additional accusations.

### Network Failure

Display a retry option.

### Missing Media

Display a fallback visual or placeholder.

The application must not crash because an optional AI-generated image or video failed.

