# 14. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The MVP is considered complete when all of the following conditions are satisfied.

## Mystery Creation

- User can enter a scenario.
- User can select difficulty.
- User can generate a mystery.
- Backend creates and stores a case.
- The case contains at least three suspects.
- The case contains multiple evidence items.
- The case has exactly one actual culprit.

## Investigation

- User can view suspects.
- User can view evidence.
- User can view the timeline.
- User can navigate between investigation sections.
- The actual culprit remains hidden.

## Accusation

- User can select a suspect.
- User can submit an accusation.
- Backend evaluates the accusation correctly.
- The case cannot be accused more than once in the MVP.

## Resolution

- Correct accusation displays a success result.
- Incorrect accusation displays a failure result.
- The actual solution is revealed.
- The solution explanation matches the generated case.

## Technical

- Frontend and backend communicate successfully.
- MongoDB stores generated cases.
- Gemini generates structured mystery content.
- API errors are handled.
- API keys remain server-side.
- The website works on desktop and mobile.

